{"kind":"event","event_id":8706,"event_uid":"01M2Q33FN9ETPT07W6BQENMDZT","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":367,"issue_uid":"01M2Q31MMK9C47SJM1FX2Y8E48","issue_short_id":"8e48","actor":"impl:1@run-176","hlc_physical_ms":1789628890793,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"020ffab223eff98f8571ba16598a41da4f5ab4f609fb3bf48058ab8ed4190ec3","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q33FN8TYAM92AH4N6ZVQB2","author":"impl:1@run-176","body":"Task 1 start. Approach: (1) M1/M2 tag grammar — strip a trailing [Mn, ...] citation tag off Proof Run: values in parse_task, record stripped commands in proof_runs and sorted clause ids in a parallel proof_run_cites; refuse unknown-clause tags beside clause_citation_violations using the same span text; a tag never counts as a citing leg. (2) M3-M6 green_at_base_lines(tasks, base_tree, timeout_s=GREEN_AT_BASE_TIMEOUT_S=30): detached worktree under tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='ultra-green-'), bash -lc with ULTRA_BASE, start_new_session + killpg on TimeoutExpired, finally worktree remove --force + prune + rmtree; one fact line per exit-0 command (prover vs guard wording), timeout line, and a final reading line. (3) M7 wiring in the --check branch of main between STALE advisories and the AUTHORING fact line, only when rc==0 and --base given.","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:08:10.792058088Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T07:08:10.793Z"}
